## Example OpenSSL commands (agent may include these in docs or CI)

> **Generate an EC private key (P-256) and CSR**
> ```bash
> openssl ecparam -name prime256v1 -genkey -noout -out server.key
> openssl req -new -key server.key -out server.csr -subj "/CN=example.com" -addext "subjectAltName = DNS:example.com, DNS:www.example.com"
> ```

> **Generate RSA 3072 key and CSR**
> ```bash
> openssl genrsa -out server.key 3072
> openssl req -new -key server.key -out server.csr -subj "/CN=example.com" -addext "subjectAltName = DNS:example.com"
> ```

> **Sign CSR with intermediate CA (openssl ca style)**
> ```bash
> openssl ca -config openssl.cnf -extensions server_cert -days 825 -notext -batch -in server.csr -out server.crt
> ```

> **Verify certificate chain**
> ```bash
> openssl verify -CAfile chain.pem server.crt
> ```

> **View cert details**
> ```bash
> openssl x509 -noout -text -in server.crt
> ```

> **Convert PEM key+cert to PKCS#12**
> ```bash
> openssl pkcs12 -export -out bundle.p12 -inkey server.key -in server.crt -certfile chain.pem
> ```

> **Create encrypted PKCS#8 key**
> ```bash
> openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -v2 aes-256-cbc -in server.key -out server.pk8.pem
> ```

> **Check TLS connection to server (s_client)**
> ```bash
> openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com -showcerts
> ```

